{
  "title": "Champagne Tower",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "type": "matrix",
  "tags": [
    "Dynamic Programming",
    "Simulation"
  ],
  "description": "Calculate how much champagne is in the (queryRow, queryGlass) glass after pouring 'poured' amount of champagne into the top glass.",
  "target": "queryRow: 1, queryGlass: 1",
  "pseudocode": "1: tower = new Array(queryRow + 1).fill(0).map((_, i) => new Array(i + 1).fill(0))\n2: tower[0][0] = poured\n3: for i from 0 to queryRow:\n4:   for j from 0 to i:\n5:     if tower[i][j] > 1:\n6:       overflow = (tower[i][j] - 1) / 2\n7:       tower[i+1][j] += overflow\n8:       tower[i+1][j+1] += overflow\n9:       tower[i][j] = 1\n10: return min(1, tower[queryRow][queryGlass])",
